  "limits": [
    "Seven integration cases retain existing logging/startup models. Native422 RX comparisons execute RX/ring/cancel/critical and actual dispatcher modes1/3; older TX-only suite retains explicit RX cuts via frozen adapter. Prior4311 math+48 M33+688 bounded generator regressions preserve their limits.",
    "Clock request/release side effects remain modeled in direct caller tests. Native copies use MMIO-only recorder; old no-op SRAM-hook negative controls preserved.",
    "Six original FP64 integration effects, external ROM APIs and synthetic peripheral/persistence/task/timing fixtures remain. Physical PLL lock/drain/live scheduling, whole source and byte equality not certified.",
    "New903 direct comparisons execute native ITM/debug cluster plus query/power28/wait helpers with delay and callback bodies controlled. Synthetic acknowledgement only; no physical MMIO/drain/concurrency proof. Seven integration cases retain startup models, so no claim they natively exercise these bodies."
